        "summary": "Port of \"Harry Potter and The Chamber of Secrets\" for Xbox and GameCube.\n\nDeveloped by EA UK and Eurocom, the GameCube, PlayStation 2 and Xbox versions of the game allow the player to access a broom and enter free-flight mode.[2] While the PlayStation 2 version allows the player to land anywhere they want, in the Xbox and GameCube version the landing zones are limited. In the GameCube version, there is an exclusive feature involving GC–GBA connectivity that allows a secret room to be opened when the two versions are connected.",
